{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM3w2Z8vvZcr4Mj4GhBj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I resolved the merge conflicts and committed the merge as `8157743`. Typecheck, lint and the TS suite pass, but `npm run test:diff` still fails 24 of 241 checks because of a blocker that existed before the merge.\n\n**What conflicted:**\n1. `test/diff/scenarios/m3.ts`: the M4 branch changed `files` into a factory that takes a protocol (`files(protocol)`), while this branch had exported the old one-argument version for M5 to use. I kept the M4 factory and exported it, and changed `test/diff/scenarios/m5.ts` to call `files('chat')`.\n2. `test/diff/index.ts`: it now loads both the M4 and M5 self-tests and runs the M1, M3, M4 and M5 scenarios together.\n3. Everything else, including the allowlist, merged without conflicts.\n\n**Results:**\n- `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` are clean.\n- `npm run test:ts` passes 7507 of 7507.\n- In `npm run test:diff`, all M5 scenarios and all self-tests pass.\n- The 24 failures are all 8 M3 review scenarios on each of the three protocols (`chat`, `responses`, `anthropic`). Each one has the same single difference: TS sends a `__roast_continue` nudge tool in its requests and the Go baseline never does. `learnings.md` already records this as a blocker on both parent branches, and the merge didn't touch that code.\n- I didn't rerun the Go build or Go tests, because no Go files changed in the merge.\n\n**Still open:** the ticket's \"harness CI job passes\" item stays unchecked until you decide the nudge question, which is open question 1 in spec 07. One option is to stop sending the nudge tool from TS. The other is to make it a numbered deliberate change and add an allowlist entry for it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":704,"cache_read_input_tokens":69259,"cache_creation":